  "key_observations_html": "<div style=\"border:1px solid #C7D8E8;border-radius:10px;padding:0.75rem 0.95rem;margin:0.1rem 0 0.55rem;background:#ffffff;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(15,23,42,0.06);\"><ul style=\"margin:0.1rem 0 0 1.05rem;padding:0;color:#1F4C67;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.45;\"><li><strong>RWA printed metrics were roughly flat this week:</strong> Distributed Value near $14.71B (-1.5% 30D) keeps on-chain RWA exposure in a holding pattern\u2014tokenization momentum is still news- and pipeline-driven until distributed value breaks range. Related: <a href=\"https://www.theblock.co/news/regulation/2026-10-19-blackrock-files-bitcoin-managed-protect-etf-downside-protection-ibit-421087\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">BlackRock files for bitcoin ETF offering downside protection and upside exposure to IBIT</a> (The Block).</li><li><strong>Tokenized U.S. Treasuries remain the institutional bridge into RWAs:</strong> adoption is strongest where products plug into cash management, collateral, and liquidity workflows. Related: <a href=\"https://thedefiant.io/news/tradfi-and-fintech/tokenized-equities-reached-3-8-billion-this-year-dwf-labs-says\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Tokenized Equities Reached $3.8 Billion This Year, DWF Labs Says</a> (The Defiant).</li><li><strong>Regulatory framing still decides product access:</strong> Clearer rules tend to unlock balance-sheet participation and collateral workflows even when aggregate on-chain totals reprice slowly. Related: <a href=\"https://www.theblock.co/news/regulation/2026-10-20-blockchain-association-clearer-rules-genius-act-421092\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Blockchain Association says Treasury\u2019s GENIUS Act rollout needs clearer DeFi, foreign issuer rules</a> (The Block).</li></ul><p class=\"takeaways__note\">Context only\u2014not investment advice. Bullets combine on-page data with recent industry headlines.</p></div><p class=\"review-note ko-disclaimer\">Key observations are AI generated and should be reviewed for accuracy.</p>",
